{"name":"English Daisy","hex":"#ffca46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"english","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spinning or rotary motion given to a ball around the vertical axis, as in pool, billiards or bowling; spin, sidespin.","An unusual or unexpected interpretation of a text or idea, a spin, a nuance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/english"},{"term":"daisy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild flowering plant of species Bellis perennis of the family Asteraceae, with a yellow head and white petals","Any of numerous other flowering plants of various species, mostly among the asterids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daisy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bellis perennis","blocks":[{"text":"Bellis perennis, the daisy, is a European species of the family Asteraceae, often considered the archetypal species of the name daisy. To distinguish this species from other plants known as daisies, it is sometimes qualified or known as common daisy, lawn daisy or English daisy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bellis_perennis_sl1.jpg/330px-Bellis_perennis_sl1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellis_perennis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bellis_perennis_001.JPG/500px-Bellis_perennis_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bellis_perennis_001.JPG/1280px-Bellis_perennis_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bellis_perennis_001.JPG/500px-Bellis_perennis_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o